==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*unnaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|unnan}}, {{cog|goh|unnan}}, {{cog|dum|onnen}} (Dutch {{m|nl|gunnen}}), Old Norse {{m|non|unna}} (Swedish {{m|sv|unna}}, Danish {{m|da|unde}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ang|/ˈun.nɑn/}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb}}

# to [[grant]] or [[bestow]] (+ ''dat'' (person) + ''gen'' (thing))
# to [[wish]]
# to [[intercede]]

